{
  "abstract": "Over half of known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. Parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$ makes the regular fifths linear in $S_{ab}$, and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$, cutting out the Branch-1 and twin-fifth sextuple surfaces. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and the first rational almost septuple of relation type $(5,2)$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness on $H$ by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. Beyond fixed-quintuple fibres, we establish Master Syzygies unifying $3$-torsion chains, Chebyshev and reflection towers, the universal $(C_0,w_1)$ osculating surface ($18/21$-compatible over $w_1(q)=(q^2-3)/(2q)$, whose sign group $V_4$ spans four $19/21$ branches), and the Vieta-jumping tower. Across all $16$ branch pairs in $(w_1,\\Lambda)$, $\\Delta_-\\Delta_+=0$ and $\\Delta_{-+}=0$ are disjoint over $\\mathbb{R}$, and on all four $19/21$ branches $\\Lambda\\in V_4\\cdot w_1(q)$ both unpaid gates descend to $Z=w_1^2$ with coprime square-free degree-$20$ numerators ($g_Z=9, g_q=39$), finite by Faltings' theorem. Vieta jumping on the master biquadratic curve is an explicit QRT translation $Q_{n-1}=[n]P_\\infty\\oplus T_0$ on the Weierstrass cubic $E_W(R^2,Z)$, yielding halving-step division laws, $2$-descent telescoping, and all-level disjointness of $\\Delta_-=0$ and $\\Delta_+=0$ away from $R\\in\\{0,\\pm 1\\}, B_W=0$. Along $Z=8(R+1)=16r^2$, Period-$4$ Laurent expansions at $R=0$ prove that $n=1$ is the unique degenerate level, while every $n\\ge 2$ yields non-degenerate canonical families in $\\mathbb{Q}(r)$ (and mirror duals over $R=1-2w^2$) satisfying $\\ge 18/21$ septuple and $\\ge 34/91$ pool conditions ($\\ge 35/91$ on $5r^2-1=\\rho^2$; exact at $n=2,3$). Shioda's height $\\hat{h}(P_\\infty)=1/2$ on the minimal K3 surface proves $\\deg_R(\\operatorname{den}(\\Lambda_n^{\\mathrm{can}}))=\\binom{n+1}{2}$ for all $n\\ge 1$ ($1\\le n\\le 12$ certified), and for $n\\in\\{2,3,4,5\\}$ each unpaid gate has genus $g\\ge 5$, finite by Faltings' theorem. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Building on Published Version 31 (review_v35_result.json), this revision incorporates all three precision improvements requested by the referee, cites Paper 90 ([32]), and adds Experiment 89 (Theorem 20(127)-(129)): (1) Applied all three precision refinements from review_v35_result.json: in Supplement Item 47, explicitly wrote the net numerator-minus-denominator degree (negative valuation at R = infinity) as -v_inf(X_W([j]P_inf)/X_W(P_inf)) = 2*(deg_R(tilde{Q}_j) - deg_R(tilde{P}_j) - ((j-1) mod 2)) = 2*1_{3|j}; parenthesized the parity exponent as P^{-((j-1) mod 2)} in Item 47 and exp88; and corrected the odd-index sub-lattice formula in exp83's docstring to Q_{2|k_n|-1} = [|k_n|]*Q_1 + [(|k_n|-1) mod 2]*T_0; (2) Added Theorem 20(127) (exp89 Part 1), factoring all 16 cross-vanishing intersections of Delta_-(R, Lambda)*Delta_+(R, Lambda) = 0 (Lambda in V_4 * w_1) with the four twin-fifth branches f_{1..4}(R, Lambda) = 0 of Delta_{-+}(R, Lambda) = 0 into 8 same-sign boundary differences +/- (w_1 -/+ 1)/(2*(w_1 +/- 1)) and 8 opposite-sign differences +/- ((2*w_1)^2 + (w_1 +/- 1)^2)/(2*(w_1^2 - 1)) (Delta = -16 < 0), proving that Delta_-*Delta_+ = 0 and Delta_{-+} = 0 are strictly disjoint over R (and Q) outside the degenerate locus w_1, Lambda in {0, +/- 1}; (3) Added Theorem 20(128) (exp89 Part 2), proving the universal root-coordinate reduction in U = (4*w_1*(w_1^2 - 1)*S + 3*w_1^4 + 14*w_1^2 - 1)/(w_1^2 - 1)^2 = sqrt(1 + u_0*c^*_-) on V_4 * w_1, strict real positivity of both unpaid gates, the chord parametrization U(w_1, t) = (w_1^2 - 1)*(25*w_1^4 + 6*w_1^2 + 1 - 8*w_1*t - t^2)/(16*w_1*(w_1^2 + 1)*t) solving 1 + u_0*c^*_- = square and 1 + c^*_-*c^*_+ = square simultaneously in Q(w_1, t), and the Universal Equi-Square Section U_eq(w_1) = U(w_1, t_{-,+}(w_1)) where both 1 + u_0*c^*_- and 1 + c^*_-*c^*_+ are squares in Q(w_1) while 1 + u_0*c^*_+ and S^2 - 4P share the square class of the genus-2 sextic P_6(Z); and (4) Added Theorem 20(129) (exp89 Part 3), proving that on all four 19/21-compatible branches Lambda in V_4 * w_1(q) of S_7^{univ}(q, Lambda), V_4-invariance and parity descend U_{univ} and both unpaid gates to Z = w_1^2 = (q^2 - 3)^2/(4*q^2) with square denominator and coprime square-free degree-20 numerators P_+(Z), P_{-+}(Z) in Z[Z] (g_Z = 9, g_{w_1} = g_{q^2} = 19, g_q = 39), establishing unconditional Faltings finiteness of each unpaid gate on all four 19/21 branches of S_7^{univ}(q, Lambda).",
